      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "Now variables actually also have types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 7.56,
          "en": "Here, I'm creating two variables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.56,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "and in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 12,
          "en": "Dart is able to infer their types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12,
          "end": 14.19,
          "en": "If you hover over your variable names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.19,
          "end": 15.57,
          "en": "you see the type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.57,
          "end": 19.23,
          "en": "and Dart knows which type will be stored in this variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 20.61,
          "en": "because it simply takes a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.61,
          "end": 23.97,
          "en": "at the value you are initially assigning to the variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.97,
          "end": 26.34,
          "en": "and uses that values type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 28.5,
          "en": "in this case here, Alignment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.5,
          "end": 30.933,
          "en": "as a type for the variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 35.4,
          "en": "If you would not assign a value initially here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.4,
          "end": 37.53,
          "en": "and you instead would only set one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.53,
          "end": 39.27,
          "en": "at a later point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.27,
          "end": 41.01,
          "en": "like this, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.01,
          "end": 44.19,
          "en": "the inferred type would be dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.19,
          "end": 46.08,
          "en": "which is a special type in Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.08,
          "end": 46.913,
          "en": "that, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.913,
          "end": 48.99,
          "en": "just means that Dart knows nothing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 48.99,
          "end": 50.76,
          "en": "about the type of this variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 50.76,
          "end": 54.45,
          "en": "and it will indeed accept all value types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 54.45,
          "end": 55.98,
          "en": "Typically, you wanna avoid this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 55.98,
          "end": 58.95,
          "en": "because that can lead to bugs in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 61.11,
          "en": "because without type information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 61.11,
          "end": 62.55,
          "en": "Dart can't ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 62.55,
          "end": 64.95,
          "en": "that you're not accidentally using the wrong type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 64.95,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "in the wrong place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 68.13,
          "en": "And therefore, in such cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 68.13,
          "end": 70.77,
          "en": "where you don't assign a value initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 70.77,
          "end": 72.96000000000001,
          "en": "you should replace the var keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 72.96000000000001,
          "end": 74.46000000000001,
          "en": "with the name of the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 76.68,
          "en": "that will be stored in that variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 76.68,
          "end": 78.9,
          "en": "Here, for example, Alignment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 78.9,
          "end": 81.93,
          "en": "with that, Dart would have more type information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 84.57,
          "en": "Though, of course, here, we would still get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 84.57,
          "end": 85.89,
          "en": "because we tell Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 85.89,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "that we wanna store a value of type Alignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "in this variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 92.193,
          "en": "but initially, we store no value in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 93.21000000000001,
          "end": 95.13,
          "en": "We would have to add a question mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 95.13,
          "end": 97.14,
          "en": "after Alignment to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 97.14,
          "end": 101.91,
          "en": "that startAlignment is either of type Alignment or null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 101.91,
          "end": 106.08,
          "en": "so that it's basically optional whether it's set or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 106.08,
          "end": 108.303,
          "en": "So a null value would be allowed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 111.53999999999999,
          "en": "Now this would lead to more errors down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 114.93,
          "en": "because begin actually doesn't want a null value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 114.93,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "and therefore, I'll get rid of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 120.15,
          "en": "and just initialize it as I did it before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 120.15,
          "end": 121.5,
          "en": "all in one step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 121.5,
          "end": 124.68,
          "en": "But it is important to know about this alternative syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 124.68,
          "end": 127.14,
          "en": "where you do explicitly set a type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 127.14,
          "end": 129.57,
          "en": "and not rely on type inference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 129.57,
          "end": 133.23,
          "en": "if you're not initializing the variable with a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 133.23,
          "end": 135.51,
          "en": "If you do that, as we're doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 135.51,
          "end": 137.79,
          "en": "using the var keyword is recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 137.79,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "because here you should indeed rely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 141.363,
          "en": "on Dart's type inference.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
